From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@hey.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 16:54:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: allow system suspend on GB20B (RTX Spark N1X)

In 620.73.04, NVIDIA replaced PDB_PROP_GPU_POWER_MANAGEMENT_UNSUPPORTED
with gpuIsPowerManagementUnsupported(), adding GB20B and GB20C to the
unsupported chip mask. RmInitPowerManagement() caches that result in
nv->is_pm_unsupported, causing both the kernel PM suspend notifier and
nvidia_suspend() to abort every s2idle transition with
NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED (0x56) on RTX Spark N1X laptops (GB20B).

Exclude GB20B from nv->is_pm_unsupported so s2idle suspend and resume
work again as they did on 615.78.08.

Upstream: https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules/issues/1577
---
 src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
--- a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
@@ -3198,7 +3198,8 @@ void RmInitPowerManagement(
             nvp->gc6_upstream_port_configured = RmConfigureUpstreamPortForRTD3(nv, NV_TRUE);
         }
 
-        nv->is_pm_unsupported = gpuIsPowerManagementUnsupported(pGpu);
+        nv->is_pm_unsupported = gpuIsPowerManagementUnsupported(pGpu) &&
+                                !IsGB20B(pGpu);
 
         // UNLOCK: release GPUs lock
         rmGpuLocksRelease(GPUS_LOCK_FLAGS_NONE, NULL);
-- 
2.56.0
